Astronomical data used by the 1930–2040 engine

VSOP87D: Bretagnon and Francou, Astronomy and Astrophysics 202 (1988).
Original coefficient files: https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/planets/vsop87/
The generator scripts/generate-vsop87.py records the SHA-256 of each input
in core/src/astronomy/vsop87_data.rs. Values use their native radians/AU units.

Moon, Mercury, Neptune, Pluto, Chiron, true lunar node and delta T: data
derived from Swiss Ephemeris, copyright Astrodienst AG, distributed here
under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
The repository LICENSE supplies the license text. Source ephemeris URLs,
versions, hashes, timescales and interpolation intervals are recorded in
the manifests under core/data/ and core/src/astronomy/. The generators
are included in this repository. Swiss Ephemeris is a data generation and
validation dependency only; no Swiss library or network service is required
by the Rust/WebAssembly runtime.

The Swiss comparison validates interpolation/implementation fidelity; for
the derived tables it is not an independent physical ephemeris model.
The validated range is 1930–2040. Approximate analytical fallbacks outside
the tables do not inherit that accuracy claim.

Pluto analytical fallback and geometric heliocentric API: Meeus,
Astronomical Algorithms, second edition, chapter 37, table 37.A.
The corrected 43-term numerical table and reference frame transformation
replace the previous incomplete table and mixed-reference-frame calculation.
